            <ArticleTitle>Polarized transilluminating dermoscopy: Bedside trichoscopic diagnosis of trichothiodystrophy.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/pde.13290</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Trichothiodystrophy is a rare autosomal recessive disorder resulting in a broad range of systemic abnormalities. Polarizing microscopy of the hair reveals the pathognomic &quot;tiger tail&quot; of alternating light and dark bands, but the need for a microscope prevents rapid bedside diagnosis. We describe a new technique for the bedside diagnosis of trichothiodystrophy using a handheld polarizing dermatoscope, precluding the need for microscopic examination.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2017 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
